From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iwci <ci@example.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:11:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] syscall, net, os/exec: WASIX processes and sockets on
 wasip1

wasix-org/go's branch `wasix` at e5fdf0eb21 (Wasmer's `golang/go`
1.25.5-wasix-1): the changes it makes under src/ to go1.25.5, without its
release workflow and wasmer.toml. GOOS stays wasip1; the standard library
calls WASIX's `wasix_32v1` imports, so `os/exec` spawns and waits for
children (proc_spawn2, proc_join) and `net` opens real sockets (sock_open,
sock_bind, sock_accept_v2, ...) where upstream wasip1 has neither.

Adapted to go1.23: //go:wasmimport takes only 32 and 64 bit integers,
floats and unsafe.Pointer there, so pointers and bools are passed as those
(here and in the patches after this one), and net builds its IPv4
multicast helper for every platform that has sockopt_posix.go, so syscall
declares IPMreq for wasip1.

The patches after this one fix what it gets wrong.
